       <h1>12-yo’s Annual ‘Diaper Drive’ Delivers 30,000 Diapers Off at Arizona Food Bank</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#philanthropy</span> <span>#community support</span> <span>#diaper drive</span> <span>#Arizona</span></div>
       <p>A 12-year-old in Arizona, identified as Sloan, has successfully completed her 5th annual 'Diaper Drive,' culminating in a substantial donation of 30,000 diapers to a food bank in Phoenix. Employees at the facility expressed surprise upon witnessing a U-Haul truck filled entirely with the donated items, a testament to the middle-schooler's dedicated efforts. Sloan has been organizing this impactful event for several years, demonstrating remarkable commitment from a young age. Her initiative addresses a critical need, as diapers are often an overlooked but essential item for families struggling with financial hardship. The sheer volume of the donation underscores the successful mobilization of community support behind Sloan's cause. This annual drive not only provides tangible relief to families but also highlights the capacity of young individuals to orchestrate significant philanthropic endeavors. The sight of a large moving truck filled with essential baby supplies arriving at the food bank thanks to a young organizer speaks volumes about the power of sustained grassroots charity.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/12-yos-annual-diaper-drive-delivers-30000-diapers-off-at-ari.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Why it matters: Youth-led initiatives demonstrate the profound impact individuals can have on community well-being through sustained effort.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the provided source material regarding the diaper drive.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.goodnewsnetwork.org/12-yos-annual-diaper-drive-dumps-30000-diapers-off-at-arizona-food-bank/" rel="noopener">Good News Network</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
