       <h1>3 Indian pacers who can consistently bowl at 150+ kmph</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Indian Cricket</span> <span>#Fast Bowlers</span> <span>#Pace</span> <span>#Umran Malik</span></div>
       <p>The search for genuine express pace remains a constant in Indian cricket, and recent performances have highlighted three young quicks who are consistently hitting the 150+ kmph mark. Umran Malik, Mayank Yadav, and Ashok Sharma have each demonstrated an impressive ability to sustain serious pace in competitive cricket, marking them as exciting prospects for the future.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/3-indian-pacers-who-can-consistently-bowl-at-150-kmph.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Umran Malik has already made a name for himself with his raw speed, often clocking speeds that trouble the best batsmen. His ability to deliver consistently quick spells has been a talking point, and he continues to refine his craft while maintaining that crucial element of express pace.</p><p>Mayank Yadav, another name generating significant buzz, has also shown that he can consistently breach the 150 kmph barrier. His performances have underlined a talent for generating high speeds, which is a rare and valuable asset in any bowling attack.</p><p>Adding to this promising trio is Ashok Sharma, who has similarly impressed with his capacity to maintain serious pace. The emergence of these three pacers suggests a bright future for Indian fast bowling, offering options that can genuinely hurry batsmen and provide a decisive edge. Their sustained speed could be a game-changer across formats.</p><p>What to watch: How these pacers develop their control alongside their raw speed.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article correctly synthesizes the information provided in the source summary.</p>
