     <article class="story single" data-beat="positive">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · The Better India · 2026-09-30 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>50 Tonnes of Waste Removed From Munak Canal | Delhi</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#community action</span> <span>#waste management</span> <span>#Delhi</span> <span>#Munak Canal</span></div>
       <p>A persistent community effort in Delhi, spearheaded by Vinay Das, has resulted in the removal of 50 metric tonnes of waste from the Munak Canal. What began with individuals cleaning by hand on September 1, 2018, has blossomed into a widespread movement. Every Sunday since its inception, Vinay Das and his team have dedicated their time to cleaning public spaces, including areas from Ashok Vihar to the Yamuna banks and the Munak Canal. Beyond waste removal, volunteers actively plant trees and care for new saplings. The initiative has successfully engaged over 1,600 children and young people, with approximately 350 individuals serving as active volunteers. The recent cleanup drives at the Munak Canal achieved the notable milestone of 50 metric tonnes of waste removed, a figure officially recorded by the MCD. For Vinay, however, the most profound reward transcends the tonnage; it's the joy of hearing a child remark, 'Bhaiya, my lane is clean today. Maa is happy.' The mission extends further, with Vinay envisioning a school for 1,500 children, where environmental protection is woven into the curriculum, fostering a new generation of environmentally conscious citizens. This ongoing commitment showcases the powerful impact of consistent community action.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/50-tonnes-of-waste-removed-from-munak-canal-delhi.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Why it matters: Consistent local action can transform public spaces and inspire environmental stewardship across generations.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately captures the details of the community movement provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://thebetterindia.com/videos/50-tonnes-of-waste-removed-from-munak-canal-delhi-12592401" rel="noopener">The Better India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
