      <a href="/feed.xml" title="RSS">RSS</a>
      <button id="tdp-theme" title="Toggle light/dark">Light</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/finance">finance</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-09-30 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>8th Pay Commission Panel Set to Visit Bengaluru and Mumbai in October 2026</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#8th Pay Commission</span> <span>#Central Government</span> <span>#Salary Revision</span> <span>#Bengaluru</span></div>
       <p>The panel for the 8th Central Pay Commission (CPC) has scheduled visits to several key cities in October 2026. Among the scheduled locations are Bengaluru in Karnataka and Mumbai in Maharashtra. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/8th-pay-commission-panel-set-to-visit-bengaluru-and-mumbai-i.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In Mumbai, the panel is specifically expected to visit the central railway department. These site visits are part of the commission’s broader effort to gather insights and assess the current remuneration structures of central government employees. </p><p>For ordinary taxpayers and employees, the proceedings of the Pay Commission directly influence future salary revisions, allowances, and pension structures. Changes recommended by the panel can impact household budgets and the overall fiscal planning of the government. </p><p>The commission’s recommendations, once finalized, will determine the financial adjustments for millions of central government workers. The focus on specific departments, such as the railways, indicates a targeted approach to understanding sector-specific challenges. </p><p>What to watch: The final recommendations of the 8th CPC panel regarding salary revisions and allowance structures.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately expands on the source details regarding the 8th CPC panel's itinerary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.livemint.com/money/personal-finance/8th-pay-commission-bengaluru-7-8-october-22-23-mumbai-visit-date-see-full-list-meeting-agenda-railways-da-salary-pension-11790766610292.html" rel="noopener">Livemint Money</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/bengaluru/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bengaluru</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
