       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · The Hindu World · 2026-09-30 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Afghanistan's Defence Ministry claims forces killed 41 insurgents crossing from Pakistan</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Afghanistan</span> <span>#Pakistan</span> <span>#Border</span> <span>#Conflict</span></div>
       <p>Kabul, Afghanistan – Afghanistan's Defence Ministry has announced that its forces killed 41 insurgents who reportedly crossed into the country from Pakistan. The ministry stated that these fighters were intercepted after entering Afghan territory.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/afghanistans-defence-ministry-claims-forces-killed-41-insurg.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The official statement from the Defence Ministry further alleged that the insurgents had crossed the border “with the support” of Pakistan. This claim suggests a cross-border operation and points to ongoing tensions between the two neighboring nations concerning border security and alleged militant activities.</p><p>Details regarding the specific location of the engagement or the exact timing of the incident were not provided in the ministry's announcement. The statement focused on the outcome of the operation and the alleged origin and support for the insurgents.</p><p>Such claims frequently highlight the complex security challenges faced in the region, particularly along the porous border shared by Afghanistan and Pakistan. Both countries have historically accused each other of harboring militants or facilitating their movement across the frontier.</p><p>The announcement by Afghanistan's Defence Ministry underscores the persistent security concerns and the vigilance of Afghan forces against perceived external threats and insurgent movements within its borders. The nature of “support” mentioned remains unspecified in the public statement.</p><p>What to watch: International reactions to the claim and any further statements from either government.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reports the claims made in the source summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/afghanistans-defence-ministry-claims-forces-killed-41-insurgents-crossing-from-pakistan/article71529796.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
