     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-09-30 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Anshuman Jha’s “Lakadbaggha 2” Set for World Premiere at Razor Reel Flanders Film Fest</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Film</span> <span>#Bollywood</span> <span>#Action</span> <span>#Film Festival</span></div>
       <p>“Lakadbaggha 2 – The Monkey Business,” the eagerly awaited sequel to the animal-lover vigilante action film “Lakadbaggha,” is scheduled to hold its World Premiere at the Razor Reel Flanders Film Fest. This prestigious event, located in Bruges, Belgium, has officially chosen the film for its 2026 programme.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/anshuman-jhas-lakadbaggha-2-set-for-world-premiere-at-razor-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This selection is particularly significant as it positions “Lakadbaggha 2” as the first Indian action franchise to achieve a World Premiere at the Razor Reel Flanders Film Fest. The festival's programming team reportedly identified the film at Marché, recognizing its potential for an international audience.</p><p>The original “Lakadbaggha” introduced audiences to a distinctive narrative centered on an animal-loving vigilante. The sequel aims to continue this storyline, building on the foundation of its predecessor. Its inclusion in a prominent international film festival underscores a growing global appreciation for diverse cinematic offerings from India.</p><p>The Razor Reel Flanders Film Fest is recognized for its curated selection of genre films, making it a fitting platform for “Lakadbaggha 2 – The Monkey Business.” This global debut is anticipated to create considerable international interest and establish the tone for the film's subsequent releases and overall reception. The premiere in Belgium offers a key opportunity for the film to connect with a worldwide audience.</p><p>What to watch: The international reception and critical buzz surrounding “Lakadbaggha 2.”</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the source information regarding the film's premiere.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/anshuman-jhas-lakadbaggha-2-the-monkey-business-becomes-1st-indian-action-franchise-to-have-world-premiere-at-razor-reel-flanders-film-fest-belgium/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
