       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPACE</span> · NASA · 2026-09-30 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Arp 78: A Peculiar Galaxy Featured on Astronomy Picture of the Day</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Space</span> <span>#Astronomy</span> <span>#Galaxy</span> <span>#APOD</span></div>
       <p>On September 30, 2026, the Astronomy Picture of the Day (APOD) will feature Arp 78, identified as a peculiar galaxy located within the constellation Aries. APOD, a project that showcases different images or photographs of the universe daily, provides a brief explanation accompanying each feature, typically authored by a professional astronomer.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/arp-78-a-peculiar-galaxy-featured-on-astronomy-picture-of-th.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The APOD initiative, under the broader umbrella of science education, serves to help the public discover the cosmos. Its daily selections aim to highlight the fascinating aspects of our universe through visual media. The specific details regarding the peculiar nature of Arp 78 or the image itself are elaborated upon within the daily feature.</p><p>This particular selection, Arp 78, draws attention to the diverse and often unusual formations found throughout the cosmos. Such galaxies are of significant interest to astronomers for understanding galactic evolution and interactions. The APOD program, with its regular updates, offers an accessible platform for both enthusiasts and the general public to engage with the latest astronomical imagery and concepts. The presentation of Arp 78 in Aries provides a specific celestial target for observation and study.</p><p>What to watch: Future APOD features for more celestial discoveries.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the provided information regarding the APOD feature.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2026-september-30-arp-78-peculiar-galaxy-in-aries/" rel="noopener">NASA</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
