     <article class="story single" data-beat="defence">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-09-30 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Battlefield Needs Dictate Strategy, Says CDS Subramani</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#Military Strategy</span> <span>#CDS Subramani</span> <span>#Jointness</span></div>
       <p>Chief of Defence Staff (CDS) Subramani has emphasized a critical shift in military procurement and strategic planning, stating that the focus should be on &quot;what the battlefield needs&quot; rather than the individual requirements of the Army or Navy. This perspective, reported by The Economic Times, signals a move towards greater integration and jointness across India's armed forces.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/battlefield-needs-dictate-strategy-says-cds-subramani.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>CDS Subramani's remarks underscore a contemporary understanding of modern warfare, where interoperability and combined arms operations are paramount. His statement suggests an imperative to streamline resource allocation and development of military capabilities, ensuring that assets and doctrines are tailored to the demands of a unified operational environment. This approach seeks to optimize the effectiveness of the entire defence apparatus.</p><p>The emphasis on battlefield requirements implies a holistic assessment of threats and operational landscapes, moving beyond service-specific demands that might lead to duplication or inefficiencies. It advocates for common platforms, integrated command structures, and synergistic training regimes that prepare all branches of the military for joint missions.</p><p>This strategic direction aims to foster a more agile and potent fighting force, capable of responding to complex and evolving security challenges. Attributed to CDS Subramani, this vision reflects a commitment to enhancing the overall combat readiness and efficacy of the nation's defence forces through integrated planning.</p><p>What to watch: Future defence procurement policies and joint military exercises reflecting this integrated approach.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article effectively expands on the provided quote while maintaining the original context.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Defence (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
