     <article class="story single" data-beat="environment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENVIRONMENT</span> · Guardian Environment · 2026-09-30 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Half a million trees to be planted in England in three years, says government</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#environment</span> <span>#tree planting</span> <span>#England</span> <span>#government policy</span></div>
       <p>England is set to see a significant environmental initiative with the planned planting of half a million trees over the next three years. Environment Secretary Angela Eagle is scheduled to make this pledge, outlining the government's commitment as part of broader efforts to enhance protection against extreme weather events. The program aims to leverage natural solutions to mitigate the impacts of a changing climate. New funding and responsibilities will be allocated to a range of partners, including mayors, local authorities, charities, and various grassroots groups. These entities will play a crucial role in restoring natural landscapes across the country. Specific focus areas include wetlands, river edges, and meadows, which are vital for ecological health and offer inherent resilience against environmental challenges. The restoration of these natural habitats is expected to provide natural flood management, helping to safeguard communities and infrastructure from inundation. Furthermore, these rejuvenated landscapes are anticipated to reduce the damage caused by periods of drought, contributing to a more resilient England. This strategic investment in nature-based solutions underscores a proactive approach to environmental management.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/half-a-million-trees-to-be-planted-in-england-in-three-years.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>What to watch: The progress of tree planting and restoration projects across England.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is a faithful summary of the provided text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/sep/30/half-million-trees-planted-england-three-years-angela-eagle" rel="noopener">Guardian Environment</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
