     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · The Hindu World · 2026-09-30 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Japan forms first national intelligence agency, eyes its own CIA</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Japan</span> <span>#intelligence</span> <span>#national security</span> <span>#geopolitics</span></div>
       <p>Japan is reportedly moving towards a significant overhaul of its intelligence gathering network, spurred by increasing discomfort over alleged foreign intelligence operations on its soil. Recent months have seen a growing demand for such a restructuring within the nation's security apparatus.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/japan-forms-first-national-intelligence-agency-eyes-its-own-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The impetus for this reform stems from allegations that several foreign powers, specifically the U.S., Russia, and China, have been conducting intelligence operations within Japan. These activities have reportedly caused considerable unease and discomfort among Japanese authorities. The perception that Japan is being utilized for foreign intelligence purposes has intensified calls for a robust, independent domestic intelligence capability.</p><p>This evolving situation underscores Japan's desire to enhance its national security and sovereignty in the face of complex international dynamics. The demand for an upgraded intelligence network reflects a strategic shift aimed at better protecting national interests and managing external influences. The move is indicative of a broader effort to strengthen Japan's position on the global stage amidst geopolitical sensitivities.</p><p>What to watch: The progress of Japan's efforts to establish and operationalize its new intelligence agency.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source material without adding unfounded claims.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/japan-forms-first-national-intelligence-agency-eyes-its-own-cia/article71529027.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
