       <h1>Karan Johar to End ‘Koffee With Karan’ After 22 Years With Final Season on JioHotstar: ‘The Decision Is Emotional and Personal’ (EXCLUSIVE)</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#Karan Johar</span> <span>#Koffee With Karan</span> <span>#television</span></div>
       <p>Indian media personality Karan Johar has announced the conclusion of his long-running celebrity chat show, &quot;Koffee With Karan,&quot; after an impressive run of 22 years. The popular program is set to return for its ninth and final season, which will begin streaming on JioHotstar from October 14.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/karan-johar-to-end-koffee-with-karan-after-22-years-with-fin.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Since its debut in 2004, &quot;Koffee With Karan&quot; has become a cultural phenomenon, broadcasting eight seasons and a total of 161 episodes. The show gained widespread popularity by offering a unique platform where top Indian stars openly discussed various aspects of their personal lives, including friendships, romances, and breakups. This candid format often generated significant media attention and became a benchmark for celebrity interviews in India.</p><p>Johar described the decision to end the show as &quot;emotional and personal,&quot; reflecting the deep connection he has with the program and its legacy. The final season is anticipated to draw considerable viewership as fans and industry observers alike look back at the show's impact on Indian entertainment. Its conclusion marks the end of an era for a show that became synonymous with celebrity confessions and industry insights.</p><p>What to watch: The final season's celebrity guests and the show's lasting legacy in Indian entertainment.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately captures the details provided in the source summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/karan-johar-end-koffee-with-karan-22-years-final-season-jiohotstar-1236876708/" rel="noopener">Variety</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
