     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-09-30 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Kuldeep Yadav Joins Elite Club with 200 ODI Wickets Milestone</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Kuldeep Yadav</span> <span>#cricket</span> <span>#ODI</span> <span>#wickets</span></div>
       <p>Indian left-arm wrist-spinner Kuldeep Yadav has etched his name into the record books, completing 200 One Day International (ODI) wickets during the second match against West Indies. The significant milestone was achieved when Yadav dismissed Keemo Paul, marking a career-defining moment for the bowler.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/kuldeep-yadav-joins-elite-club-with-200-odi-wickets-mileston.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This achievement places Kuldeep Yadav among an elite group of Indian bowlers, as he becomes the third-fastest Indian to reach the 200-wicket mark in ODI cricket. His consistent performance and ability to pick crucial wickets have been a hallmark of his career, making him a vital asset to the Indian team's bowling attack.</p><p>The context of this achievement in the ongoing series against West Indies further highlights his impact. Reaching such a significant milestone against an international opponent underscores his skill and dedication on the global stage. Yadav's unique wrist-spin variations have often troubled batsmen, and this record is a testament to his effectiveness in the 50-over format.</p><p>Fans and pundits alike will be watching to see how quickly he climbs further up the all-time wicket-takers list for India, continuing to break records and solidify his legacy in white-ball cricket. His journey to 200 wickets is a strong indicator of his sustained form and potential for even greater achievements.</p><p>What to watch: Kuldeep Yadav's continued impact in upcoming matches and series.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article correctly identifies the bowler and the milestone mentioned in the source.</p>
