       <h1>Navarro opens up on health struggles that caused 'deep anger' on court</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tennis</span> <span>#health</span> <span>#athlete</span> <span>#mental health</span></div>
       <p>American athlete Emma Navarro has candidly discussed her long-running health problems, shedding light on the profound impact they had on both her personal life and professional career. Navarro revealed that she experienced significant weight loss, persistent fatigue, and recurrent episodes of dizziness, which severely affected her well-being.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/navarro-opens-up-on-health-struggles-that-caused-deep-anger-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>These ongoing health challenges were not confined to her personal life but also manifested on the tennis court. Navarro specifically stated that these difficulties left her &quot;feeling deep internal anger&quot; during matches, underscoring the emotional and psychological toll her condition took. Her openness provides a rare glimpse into the unseen struggles that professional athletes can face, beyond their public performances.</p><p>In a recent statement, Navarro shared a positive update, indicating that she has now &quot;gained her life back.&quot; This suggests a period of recovery and resilience, as she has evidently overcome or is managing her health issues more effectively. Her journey highlights the importance of addressing athlete well-being comprehensively, encompassing both physical and mental health aspects, and serves as an example of perseverance in the face of adversity.</p><p>What to watch: Emma Navarro's return to full form and her performance in future tournaments.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the provided source material without adding extraneous or unbacked information.</p>
