     <article class="story single" data-beat="environment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENVIRONMENT</span> · Guardian Environment · 2026-09-30 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>New Research Highlights Insects' Crucial Ecosystem Roles Beyond Food</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#insects</span> <span>#ecosystems</span> <span>#conservation</span> <span>#biodiversity</span></div>
       <p>Insects, often perceived primarily as a food source for other creatures, play far more critical and diverse roles within ecosystems than previously emphasized, according to a new study published on Wednesday in Nature Reviews Biodiversity. The research highlights how these &quot;little things that run the world&quot; provide essential functions such as protection, sanitation, and even shelter to a wide array of vertebrates.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/new-research-highlights-insects-crucial-ecosystem-roles-beyo.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>For many species, including birds, bats, reptiles, amphibians, and various mammals, insects are indispensable beyond their nutritional value. The study sheds light on the multifaceted ways these invertebrates support and sustain vertebrate life. This includes, but is not limited to, creating microhabitats, aiding in the decomposition of organic matter, and offering defensive mechanisms through their presence or by-products.</p><p>The findings underscore the profound interconnectedness of ecosystems and position insects as a priority for conservation efforts. Recognizing their broad contributions — from maintaining ecological balance through sanitation to directly influencing the survival and well-being of other animal groups by providing shelter and protection — is vital. This research reinforces the urgent need to protect insect populations globally, ensuring the health and stability of the entire ecological web.</p><p>What to watch: Future conservation strategies prioritizing insect populations.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article faithfully summarizes the research findings regarding insect ecosystem services.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/sep/30/insects-ecosystems-conservation" rel="noopener">Guardian Environment</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
