     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · The Hindu World · 2026-09-30 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Pakistan Deputy PM reaffirms its commitment to open, inclusive and constructive SCO Chairmanship</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Pakistan</span> <span>#SCO</span> <span>#Diplomacy</span> <span>#International Relations</span></div>
       <p>Islamabad, Pakistan – Pakistan's Deputy Prime Minister, Mr. Dar, has reaffirmed the nation's commitment to an “open, inclusive and constructive” Chairmanship of the Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO). The statement underscores Pakistan's diplomatic approach to leading the regional body.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/pakistan-deputy-pm-reaffirms-its-commitment-to-open-inclusiv.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During his remarks, Mr. Dar highlighted the central theme chosen for Pakistan's tenure as SCO Chair: 'Turning Vision into Action: Connectivity, Innovation, and Shared Prosperity'. This theme outlines the strategic priorities Pakistan intends to pursue during its leadership role.</p><p>The emphasis on “open, inclusive and constructive” engagement suggests a focus on fostering cooperation and dialogue among member states on various regional and international issues. It indicates a desire to promote collective solutions and strengthen the organization's collaborative framework.</p><p>The theme itself, 'Connectivity, Innovation, and Shared Prosperity', points towards key areas of focus. 'Connectivity' likely refers to enhancing regional links, including infrastructure and trade routes. 'Innovation' could encompass technological advancements and new approaches to common challenges. 'Shared Prosperity' suggests efforts to ensure equitable economic growth and development across the SCO member nations.</p><p>Pakistan's leadership aims to translate these guiding principles into tangible outcomes, fostering a more integrated and prosperous region under the SCO umbrella. The Deputy Prime Minister's reaffirmation sets the tone for the country's diplomatic efforts in its current role.</p><p>What to watch: Specific initiatives or proposals Pakistan may introduce under its SCO Chairmanship.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source material and provides reasonable, non-factual context.</p>
