     <article class="story single" data-beat="space">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPACE</span> · NASA · 2026-09-30 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Powerful Storms Continue to Prowl the Pacific</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Hurricanes</span> <span>#Pacific</span> <span>#NASA</span></div>
       <p>The Pacific Ocean is currently experiencing a period of heightened storm activity, with Hurricanes Polo and Nolo demonstrating significant power. These recent hurricanes have been notable for the destructive effects they delivered ashore, impacting coastal areas within the vast northeastern and central Pacific regions. The presence and intensity of both Polo and Nolo underscore what is being characterized as an active storm season for this part of the globe.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/powerful-storms-continue-to-prowl-the-pacific.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The repeated occurrence of powerful systems such as these highlights the dynamic nature of weather patterns in the Pacific basin. While specific dates or mission details are not provided in this summary, the focus remains on the observable impact of these large-scale atmospheric events. The destructive effects reaching land emphasize the critical importance of monitoring such storms, particularly for communities situated along the Pacific coastlines.</p><p>The combined force of Hurricanes Polo and Nolo contributes to a broader understanding of the meteorological conditions driving this active season. Their impact serves as a reminder of the continuous natural forces at play, shaping environments and posing challenges to human settlements in their path. The ongoing activity in these Pacific zones indicates a sustained period of vigilance for weather watchers and affected populations.</p><p>What to watch: The continued development of storm systems in the Pacific.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the provided source summary without introducing external claims.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/powerful-storms-continue-to-prowl-the-pacific/" rel="noopener">NASA</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
