       <h1>Shubman Gill's Record Double Hundred Powers India To Their Highest Successful ODI Run Chase</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#ODI</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#West Indies</span></div>
       <p>India has asserted its dominance in the three-match One Day International (ODI) series against the West Indies, securing an unassailable 2-0 lead. This commanding position was cemented following a decisive victory in the second match of the series.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/shubman-gills-record-double-hundred-powers-india-to-their-hi.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The Indian team delivered a strong performance, effectively crushing the West Indies by eight wickets. This significant win in the second encounter ensured that India clinched the series with one match still remaining. The comprehensive nature of the victory underscores India's current strength and strategic execution in the limited-overs format.</p><p>The early conclusion of the series in India's favor highlights their consistent performance and ability to adapt to game conditions. With the overall series result now confirmed, the upcoming final match will provide an opportunity for both teams to conclude the contest, though its outcome will not alter India's series triumph. This successful campaign against the West Indies marks another notable achievement for the Indian cricket team on the international stage, demonstrating their form and depth.</p><p>What to watch: The final match of the series as India seeks to complete a clean sweep.</p>
       
