     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-09-30 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>TVK-Left Rift Widens Ahead of Tamil Nadu By-Polls; CPI(M) to Field Own Candidates</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Tamil Nadu</span> <span>#Politics</span> <span>#By-polls</span> <span>#TVK</span></div>
       <p>A significant political development has emerged in Tamil Nadu as the rift between the TVK and the Left parties has reportedly widened. This escalation comes ahead of the upcoming by-polls in the state, signaling a potential shift in the political landscape.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/tvk-left-rift-widens-ahead-of-tamil-nadu-by-polls-cpim-to-fi.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Sources indicate that the Communist Party of India (Marxist), CPI(M), has decided to field its own candidates in the impending elections. This move by the CPI(M) underscores the deepening divisions within what was once a collaborative political front. The decision highlights a breakdown in alliance dynamics, particularly concerning seat-sharing or strategic coordination for the by-polls.</p><p>The widening chasm between the TVK and the Left, specifically the CPI(M)'s independent electoral strategy, suggests a more fragmented contest in the by-elections. Such a scenario could lead to multi-cornered fights, potentially altering the electoral outcomes and requiring parties to recalibrate their campaign approaches. The by-polls are often seen as a litmus test for broader political trends and alliances.</p><p>This development will undoubtedly draw close scrutiny from political observers, who will be keen to assess the impact of these fractured alliances on voter sentiment and the overall distribution of power in the state. The by-polls are set to become a key indicator of the evolving political equations in Tamil Nadu.</p><p>What to watch: The performance of independent CPI(M) candidates in the by-polls and the subsequent impact on state politics.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the source summary without adding extraneous information.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/video/tvk-left-rift-widens-ahead-of-tamil-nadu-by-polls-cpim-to-field-own-candidates-ytvd-3006280-2026-09-30?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
