       <h1>Vice President Highlights Emerging Technologies for Accurate Defence Land Management, Interacts with IDES Probationers</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Vice President</span> <span>#Defence Land Management</span> <span>#Emerging Technologies</span> <span>#IDES Probationers</span></div>
       <p>The Vice President recently highlighted the crucial role of emerging technologies in achieving accurate defence land management. This emphasis underscores the government's commitment to leveraging advanced tools for efficient and precise administration of defence properties. The statement was made during an interaction with probationers from the Indian Defence Estates Service (IDES).</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/vice-president-highlights-emerging-technologies-for-accurate.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The Vice President stressed the importance of accuracy in defence land management, a critical aspect for national security and resource optimization. Emerging technologies, while not specified in detail, are seen as instrumental in enhancing the precision, transparency, and accountability of land records and management processes within the defence sector. This focus aims to streamline operations and ensure optimal utilization of defence assets.</p><p>The interaction with IDES probationers indicates a direct engagement with the future administrators of defence estates. It serves to impress upon them the significance of their role and the imperative to adopt modern technological solutions in their work. The Vice President’s address likely aimed to inspire these new recruits to embrace innovation and precision in their upcoming responsibilities.</p><p>This initiative reflects a strategic move towards modernizing the administrative frameworks governing defence land. By advocating for emerging technologies, the Vice President points towards a future where data-driven approaches and advanced tools are central to effective defence land management.</p><p>What to watch: Future policy directives or initiatives detailing specific technological adoptions for defence land management.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the Vice President's interaction and stated priorities.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Defence (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
