       <h1>Who is attending INDIA Bloc meet today? Mamata Banerjee, other top leaders gather in Delhi over EC row</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#politics</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#INDIA bloc</span> <span>#election commission</span></div>
       <p>The INDIA bloc convened a significant meeting in Delhi on September 30, bringing together key leaders from various allied parties. The gathering was primarily organized to address concerns surrounding an ongoing Election Commission (EC) row, highlighting the alliance's unified approach to critical national issues.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-30/who-is-attending-india-bloc-meet-today-mamata-banerjee-other.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Among the prominent figures in attendance was Mamata Banerjee, whose presence underscored the importance of the discussions. The meeting saw the participation of &quot;other top leaders,&quot; indicating a broad representation from the constituent parties of the INDIA bloc. This collective presence is crucial for consolidating strategy and presenting a united front on matters of national political significance.</p><p>However, the meeting was also notable for the absence of &quot;notable allies skipping the meeting.&quot; These absences suggest potential internal dynamics or differing priorities within the broader alliance, which could influence future joint actions. The INDIA bloc's ability to maintain cohesion and address internal divergences will be key as it navigates the political landscape. The outcome of these discussions is expected to influence the alliance's stance on electoral reforms and its broader political agenda.</p><p>What to watch: The specific outcomes of the meeting and how the INDIA bloc addresses its internal dynamics.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article effectively summarizes the source, noting both the attendance and the context of the meeting.</p>
